cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software/data in your research, please cite it as follows."
title: "Fault Signatures in the Spike Stream of a Closed-Loop Neuronal Culture Substrate"
abstract: >-
  Actuator faults are detectable from the spike stream of a closed-loop
  neuronal culture substrate on a Unitree G1 humanoid in MuJoCo simulation.
  AUC 0.890-0.995, lead time 0.61-3.02s, topographic localization consistent
  across substrates, seeds, and terrains. The culture is an informing sensor
  whose fault signatures transfer across substrates but whose authority to
  compensate remains bounded.
keywords:
  - closed-loop neural culture
  - fault detection
  - spiking substrate
  - humanoid locomotion
  - topographic readout
  - mutual information
  - lead time
